    {
      "beat_id": "B00",
      "act": "ASK",
      "narration_text": "Every picture you have ever seen made by an AI started life as pure static. Random dots. Nothing. This is Humanitarians AI, and today we find out how a machine turns a screenful of mess into a picture — using a real one, built from scratch, that you can watch working.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type-on",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "greeting": "Show me how it works.",
            "topic": "HOW PICTURE MACHINES WORK",
            "segment": "Static Into Pictures",
            "command": "Explain how a diffusion model turns random noise into data, using a real from-scratch implementation. Start with the trick that makes it possible, and show me the numbers at every step.",
            "runningText": "opening the notebook…",
            "folderLabel": "@HumanitariansAI",
            "output": [
              "first: wreck a picture on purpose",
              "then: learn to spot the mess",
              "finally: take the mess back off"
            ]
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B00.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-12T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 19.6,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B00.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 17.77,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B00.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:ClaudeComposerAsk",
        "at": "2026-10-12T13:09:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "PICTURE",
      "narration_text": "We need something to make, so here is our picture. Not a cat, not a face — just a spiral of dots. Small enough that you can see every single one, which means you can see absolutely everything that happens to it.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "OUR PICTURE",
            "headline": "A spiral made of dots.",
            "kicker": "small enough to watch every step"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-12T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16.2,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.01,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-10-12T13:09:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "SPRINKLE",
      "narration_text": "Now the strange first move. We wreck it. On purpose. Take the spiral and sprinkle a tiny bit of mess over it. Then sprinkle a tiny bit more. And again. Two hundred times.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "KidSprinkle",
          "props": {},
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B02.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-12T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 12.7,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.65,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:KidSprinkle",
        "at": "2026-10-12T13:09:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "GONE",
      "narration_text": "By the end, only 8 percent of the spiral is left. Everything you could recognise is gone. It is a round fuzzy cloud, and it looks exactly like television static.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "ALL GONE",
            "headline": "Only about 8% of the picture survives.",
            "kicker": "two hundred tiny sprinkles, and no spiral"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B03.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-12T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 11.5,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.45,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-10-12T13:09:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "IDEA",
      "narration_text": "And here is the whole idea, in one sentence. Making a mess is easy — but we wrote down exactly how much mess we added each time. So the mess is not random to us. We have the recipe.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "THE BIG IDEA",
            "headline": "Wrecking it is easy. And we kept the recipe.",
            "kicker": "if you know how it was broken, you can learn to unbreak it"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B04.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-12T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 15.0,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.84,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-10-12T13:09:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "QUESTION",
      "narration_text": "So we show the machine a messy picture, and we ask it one question. Not, what is this a picture of. Just: which bit of this is the mess?",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "illustrate",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "KidMessSpotter",
          "props": {},
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B05.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-12T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 11.2,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.51,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:KidMessSpotter",
        "at": "2026-10-12T13:09:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "WHY",
      "narration_text": "That is a much easier question, and it is the clever part of the whole thing. The machine never needs to know it is looking at a spiral. It only needs to point at the sprinkles.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "WHY THAT HELPS",
            "headline": "Spot the mess, and you can take a little off.",
            "kicker": "an easy question, asked two hundred times"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B06.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-12T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 13.8,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.15,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-10-12T13:09:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "act": "REVERSE",
      "narration_text": "So that is what we do. Start with nothing but static. Ask: where is the mess? Brush a tiny bit of it away. Then ask again. Two hundred times.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "KidUnsprinkle",
          "props": {},
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B07.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-12T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 11.2,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.28,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:KidUnsprinkle",
        "at": "2026-10-12T13:09:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "act": "MAGIC",
      "narration_text": "And a spiral appears. Not the one we started with — that one is long gone. A brand new spiral, built out of random dots by a machine that only ever learned to spot mess.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "A SPIRAL NOBODY DREW",
            "headline": "Out of pure static, a new picture.",
            "kicker": "nothing of the original was left to copy"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B08.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-12T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 13.5,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.9,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-10-12T13:09:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "act": "HOMEWORK",
      "narration_text": "Now, should we believe any of this? The people who built it asked the same thing. So they worked out the maths by hand, then had the computer check it a completely different way, by counting.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "stagger",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "KidTwoWaysCheck",
          "props": {
            "worstErr": "1.5e-07"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B09.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-12T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 13.8,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.88,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:KidTwoWaysCheck",
        "at": "2026-10-12T13:09:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "act": "HONEST",
      "narration_text": "They were honest about the hard bits too. While learning, the machine's score stops improving at about 0.3, and never reaches zero. That is not a fault. Some of the mess genuinely cannot be guessed, by anyone, ever.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "AN HONEST NUMBER",
            "headline": "It never gets a perfect score. It cannot.",
            "kicker": "some sprinkles are simply unguessable"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B10.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-12T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 14.6,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B10.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.78,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B10.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-10-12T13:09:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B11",
      "act": "JUDGE",
      "narration_text": "Then they brought in a judge — a way of scoring how close the made-up spirals are to real ones. Lower is better.",
