    {
      "beat_id": "B16",
      "act": "TRADEOFF",
      "narration_text": "With the dial at zero it ignores you completely — 48 percent right, which is just a coin flip. Turn it to one and it gets the right shape 99.8 percent of the time. Turn it higher and it is perfect, every time.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "TURNING IT UP",
            "headline": "From a coin flip to never wrong.",
            "kicker": "so why not turn it all the way up?"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B16.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-12T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16.5,
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B16.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.82,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media\\B16.mp4",
        "filled_by": "remotion:IdxStatement",
        "at": "2026-10-12T13:09:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B17",
      "act": "COST",
      "narration_text": "Because look at the second bar. As obedience goes up, variety goes down — from 0.95 all the way to 0.50. The shapes get more and more alike. You asked for exactly what you wanted, and you got it, over and over again.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "fade",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "IdxStatement",
          "props": {
            "eyebrow": "WHAT IT COSTS",
            "headline": "More obedient. Less interesting.",
            "kicker": "there is no setting that gives you both"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B17.mp4",
            "at": "2026-10-12T00:00:00"
          }
        }
      },
      "estimated_duration_s": 16.5,
